# These logs are append-only: every run adds lines at the end and never edits
# existing ones. Two check-in runs finishing close together therefore both
# append at the same position, which git's default merge treats as a conflict
# (this broke a run on 2026-08-27). The built-in `union` merge driver keeps
# BOTH sides' lines instead of conflicting, which is exactly the desired
# semantics for an append-only log.
*.jsonl merge=union
